00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.840
episode

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.840
"With Tears of Dignity..."

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.820
What is all this commotion?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.590
I can't take it anymore, Your Majesty!

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.050
How am I supposed to make any
sense of it, if you're crying?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.710
Now, tell me what happened.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.320
Your Majesty, please banish that brat and all those who side with her from court!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.470
Yes, every last one of them!

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.680
Where is this coming from, all of the sudden?

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.140
Your Majesty is so calm, because you
are unaware of what is happening!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.860
That brat ignored the order from her Austrian homeland...

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:12.480
No, Your Majesty's order...!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.940
Not only that, she openly ignored it,

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.080
Your Majesty!

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.030
<i>How can this be?!</i>

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:22.300
<i>No one has ever dared to defy my orders.</i>

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:28.310
<i>In fact, everyone is falling over themselves
to earn even the slightest bit of my favor.</i>

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:35.960
<i>Yet, my grandson's puny bride has openly ignored
the order of Louis XV, the King of France?!</i>

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:45.020
<i>It's true! That redheaded twerp openly ignored
Your Majesty's order in front of all the nobles!</i>

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.140
Minister of Foreign Affairs!

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.890
Bring me the Minister of Foreign Affairs!

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.720
I should have known it was you.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.370
That was quite an act you put on.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.700
What brings you here, Duke Orléans?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:25.800
At the rate this match is going,
Antoinette will probably win.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.520
What?!

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.590
Well, wouldn't you say so?

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.170
His Majesty is at an advanced age.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:37.690
If something were to happen to His Majesty,
the one who would ascend to the throne,

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.650
would be that dimwitted locksmith.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:48.360
If the Dauphin becomes king,
that Austrian-born brat will become queen.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:54.250
If the new king is controlled by that brat...

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.820
You'll be hastily sent away to Bastille's prison,

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.290
or worst case...

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:03.880
...Be executed.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:04.840
Executed?!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.100
Then, what do you suggest I do, Duke Orléans?

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.700
If the Dauphin is no longer,
Antoinette will be sent back to Austria.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.360
If the Dauphin is no longer,
that would mean you will...

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:37.470
What do you say, Madame du Barry?

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:41.970
Cooperate with me and you will keep your
rank and position for years to come.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.610
The Dauphin is attending the
annual fox hunt tomorrow.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:55.660
If his gun were to explode during the hunt
and he died, no one would suspect a thing.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:59.190
Such a ruthless person...

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.320
Do you agree?

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:07.610
When the Dauphin is dead, you will urge
the King to make me his successor.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:15.540
Which means, starting tomorrow you
and I will rule France together!

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:30.520
Make sure you do not forget the secret
arrangement, we made on this day.

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.790
Ambassador Mercy of the Austrian Empire.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:43.770
I am here to deliver an official message from the French Minister of Foreign Affairs.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:46.570
In Madame du Barry's private quarters?

00:07:47.080 --> 00:07:48.540
That is correct.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>A special meeting with His Majesty...</i>

00:07:55.620 --> 00:08:00.250
<i>Not in the official audience chambers, but in Madame du Barry's private quarters...</i>

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.830
<i>It must be about Lady Antoinette...</i>

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.560
<i>At about the same time,</i>

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:10.260
<i>in the cellar of Palais-Royal,
the residential palace of Duke Orléans...</i>

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.060
Well? Is it finished?

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:19.430
Yes, here it is.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:31.030
Whoever pulls the trigger of this gun will certainly die from the gunpowder explosion, loaded inside the bullet.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.780
Well done.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.870
I must reward you for your work.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.850
Thank you!

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:54.340
Replace the Dauphin's gun with that gun.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.380
Do not fail!

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.030
Yes!

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:24.920
Count Mercy, I have summoned you today to
discuss matters concerning the Dauphine.

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:26.370
Y-Yes.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.150
I ask that you make the Princess understand...

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:34.440
...that if she does not correct her behavior towards Madame du Barry,

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.210
there will be grave consequences.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.590
Yes!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.220
Say, Count Mercy...

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.280
If she enrages His Majesty any further...

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:49.390
Even I will not be able to defend
Lady Antoinette any longer.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:52.370
You, defend the Princess, Madame?

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:53.200
Why, yes.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:56.870
The Dauphine took to heart the foolish
gossip that has been spread about me,

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:00.010
and harbors an unfounded hostility
towards me because of it.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.750
I was just explaining this to His Majesty,
as I have been doing all long.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.710
Indeed.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:13.130
In that case, Madame du Barry,
I-I am truly grateful for your actions...

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.470
<i>Well, now...</i>

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:28.270
<i>What could I possibly say to Lady Antoinette that would persuade her...?</i>

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:09.040
Your Highness, the fox is approaching.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:10.980
R-Right.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.120
Damn her!

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.470
As always, you are {more of
a sharpshooter}a better
shot than I am, Oscar.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:32.500
Thank you.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:33.670
It was a lucky shot.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:37.610
Oscar!

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:38.210
Yes?

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:42.510
The Dauphin does not shoot,
because you shoot the prey first.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.910
Restrain yourself!

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.850
This time, I won't lose to you, Oscar.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.690
Your Highness, over there.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.470
Please hurry, Your Highness.

00:12:12.470 --> 00:12:13.420
I-I know.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.880
<i>You moron! Hurry up and pull the trigger!</i>

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:19.840
<i>Now!</i>

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:48.670
Easy...

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.040
Your Highness, are you hurt?

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.410
How careless of me. Such a blunder...

00:12:55.410 --> 00:12:59.240
Oscar, don't tell Antoinette
I fell from my horse, all right?

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.250
That Dauphin has the Devil's own luck!

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.580
Someday...

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:05.280
Someday, I will send him to his grave!

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.250
Never! Never!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.250
I refuse!

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.640
However, Your Highness...

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:19.870
If someone must speak to Madame du Barry,
why don't you speak to her?

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.820
I'll never do it!

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.610
Well then, Your Highness, do as you please!

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:34.750
Just remember that the French-Austrian alliance
that your mother, Lady Maria Theresa,

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:40.280
has spent her entire life forging will be broken,
solely due to Your Highness' selfish actions!

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.120
My mother in Austria...

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:54.440
Oscar, what are your thoughts on this matter?

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:56.690
Count Mercy is speaking the truth.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:59.690
I may be speaking out of line,
but please allow me to say this.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:04.510
Your Highness has been goaded
into being stubborn by your aunts,

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:06.680
and is now caught in a petty rivalry of women.

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:11.250
As a result, all of Europe could be engaged in war.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:15.660
If that should happen, thousands...
Tens of thousands of people will die.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.580
A petty rivalry fueled by stubbornness, you say?

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:20.960
Yes, that is correct.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:25.380
And because of that,
all of Europe could be engaged in war...

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:44.320
To me, it hardly seems like something
the future Queen of France would do.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:52.520
Count Mercy, I promise.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:55.110
That woman...

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:56.950
Just once...

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:59.110
Just once, I will speak to her!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:01.530
But, but...!

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.880
I am doing this against my own will!

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:09.130
I am doing this,

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.370
solely for the sake of
my mother in Austria.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.880
It is for my mother's sake!

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:16.250
Count Mercy, do you understand?!

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:26.750
<i>Early July, 1771.</i>

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:31.280
<i>From the maid quarters to the stable corners...</i>

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.820
<i>All of Paris was clamoring in excitement and anticipation.</i>

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.140
It's happening at tonight's party.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:41.290
My, Lady Antoinette is finally giving
in to Madame du Barry, isn't she?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.580
Such a pity! Such an awful pity!

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.950
What a shame, Oscar.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:49.550
Looks like even Lady Antoinette had to
back down, faced with the King's power.

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:50.470
André!

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.230
Do you understand?

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:05.200
When that happens, you will
say this to Madame du Barry...

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.900
Yes, I know!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.340
We've practiced it four times already!

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.600
Four times!

00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:13.530
Then, I wish you success tonight.

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.040
<i>Lady Antoinette...</i>

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.220
She's probably playing card
games, right about now.

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:46.200
You have a good hand.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.040
After the game ends, at exactly 8:30,

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:52.640
Count Mercy will finally approach
Madame du Barry to talk.

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.540
Such a well-played game.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:07.630
Next time, perhaps you and I could play a game?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.030
.and then, she's going to appear as
if it were all a coincidence.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:15.470
Presenting Her Royal Highness,
Lady Marie Antoinette!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.190
Good evening, Countess Maurois.

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.910
It certainly is a lively party tonight.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.870
Marquise Rosen, please enjoy
and have a pleasant time.

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.650
Good evening, Count Mercy.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:13.610
Yes, I am pleased to see
Your Highness is in fine heath.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.000
Your Highness!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.680
It's her aunt, Lady Adélaïde!

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:37.130
Come!

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.750
It's already time for you to leave!

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.890
Please wait, I still haven't...

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:44.900
You must wait for His Majesty in your room!

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:46.290
His Majesty?

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.060
Yes! Come, hurry!

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:50.120
Lady Antoinette!

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:53.070
Mercy!

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:08.080
I knew those aunts would pull something.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.550
And sure enough...!

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:26.100
Count Mercy!

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:30.740
Please also explain to His Majesty that what
happened today was completely unintentional!

00:19:30.740 --> 00:19:33.040
Your Highness, please do not worry.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.910
I, Mercy, will make sure he knows.

00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:38.900
Next time...

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:41.240
Next time, I will make sure I speak to her...

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:48.750
<i>The new year, January 1, 1772.</i>

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:51.890
<i>All the nobles from across France...</i>

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:56.170
<i>...visited the Palace of Versailles to deliver their new year greetings.</i>

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.800
The Honorable Marquise Rovere!

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:03.430
The Honorable Duchess de Guéméné!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.000
The Honorable Marquise Lombaire!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.250
Happy New Year.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.010
Happy New Year, Lady Antoinette.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.900
The Honorable Countess du Barry!

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:42.970
Happy New Year.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:46.510
There are a lot of people at Versailles today.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.460
Lady Antoinette!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.670
<i>There are a lot of people at Versailles today...</i>

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>There are a lot of people at Versailles today...</i>

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:25.680
<i>There are a lot of people at Versailles today...</i>

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.250
I lost!

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:47.160
Oscar...!

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:51.440
I have now addressed her once...

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:53.910
But I'll never do it again!

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:57.280
I'll never speak a single word
to that woman ever again!

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:01.020
The French Court has gone corrupt.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:05.220
The wife of the heir to the throne
has lost to a prostitute!

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:12.370
<i>Such a prideful and dignified lady...</i>

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:14.940
<i>She was born to be a Queen.</i>

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:18.000
<i>In her heart, she is already the Queen of France.</i>

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:25.200
<i>Lady Antoinette, I, Oscar, swear by my sword to
serve Your Highness for as long as I live.</i>

00:22:27.950 --> 00:22:32.330
To be continued

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:43.550
ai ga kurushimi nara

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:43.550
ai ga kurushimi nara

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:43.550
If to love is to suffer,

00:22:37.670 --> 00:22:43.550
If to love is to suffer,

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:48.890
